²/(2 E Phi_xx³), and mu(dt)=gamma′(t)dt. For 0<t<1, 2 gamma′ E Phi_xx³≥gamma(t)² E Phi_xx⁴/1000>0. Only gamma′(0)≥0 is asserted at zero. Since E Phi_xx²=1 and Phi_xx>=0, moment Cauchy–Schwarz gives E Phi_xx³<=sqrt(E Phi_xx⁴)<=E Phi_xx⁴. Hence gamma′(t)>=gamma(t)²/2000 for 0<t<1, and mu((r,s])>=(s-r)gamma(r)²/2000 for 0<r<s<1.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"field:d26c47ace9300bdbfba7573c0f1455b70611467ff1db175e0027825eb9515c1a","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22scalar.smooth_positive_density%22%2C%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22scalar.smooth_positive_density%22%2C%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993e